&lt;p&gt;Knowing how to use your computer is one thing, but knowing how to get the most out of it is another. Why might you need more RAM or a GPU? What is the BIOS? And how does &amp;ldquo;the cloud&amp;rdquo; fit in? Whether you have a brand new computer or you want to make the most of the one you already have, this workshop will help you answer these questions and more. We&amp;rsquo;ll go into the terminology and the capabilities, limitations, and potential of your computer, whether it&amp;#39;s a PC, Mac, Chromebook, or something else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attendees are encouraged, but not required, to bring a laptop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Independent journalism is vital to informed public debate, but can it survive under authoritarian conditions? Join the Sakıp Sabancı Center for Turkish Studies for a conversation with Ann Cooper and Diego Cupolo. Drawing on their extensive professional experience, the speakers will discuss the challenges of journalism in repressive and contested information environments, including restrictions on press freedom, ethical and professional dilemmas faced by reporters and editors, and the opportunities and vulnerabilities of digital journalism.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
