&lt;p&gt;Esta conferencia m&amp;eacute;dica internacional virtual re&amp;uacute;ne a aliados del Columbia University Irving Medical Center y de la Universidad Nacional Pedro Henr&amp;iacute;quez Ure&amp;ntilde;a para una conversaci&amp;oacute;n intercultural sobre la salud mental y respiratoria. La UNPHU abordar&amp;aacute; la depresi&amp;oacute;n y la ansiedad, incluyendo el estigma en torno a la salud mental y las perspectivas culturales. Por su parte, CUIMC destacar&amp;aacute; el asma y el papel de los trabajadores comunitarios de la salud en la conexi&amp;oacute;n entre la educaci&amp;oacute;n, la atenci&amp;oacute;n m&amp;eacute;dica y los recursos comunitarios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La Dra. Kersy Yoirys Medina F&amp;eacute;liz&lt;/strong&gt; es psiquiatra y docente de la UNPHU, con formaci&amp;oacute;n avanzada en Medicina Interna, Psiquiatr&amp;iacute;a, terapia familiar y de pareja, y adicciones. Actualmente se desempe&amp;ntilde;a como gerente del Departamento de Salud Mental del Hospital Docente Vinicio Calventi y cuenta con amplia experiencia en la atenci&amp;oacute;n cl&amp;iacute;nica, la docencia universitaria y el liderazgo en salud mental. Como ponente de la UNPHU en esta conferencia virtual internacional, presentar&amp;aacute; sobre la depresi&amp;oacute;n y la ansiedad, con &amp;eacute;nfasis en el estigma de la salud mental y las perspectivas culturales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La Dra&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Luz Adriana Matiz &lt;/strong&gt;es profesora de Pediatr&amp;iacute;a en Columbia University Irving Medical Center y directora m&amp;eacute;dica del Centro de Navegaci&amp;oacute;n de Salud Comunitaria de NewYork Presbyterian Hospital, donde lidera programas de navegadores de pacientes y trabajadores comunitarios de la salud a nivel del sistema. Cuenta con reconocimiento nacional por su experiencia en el manejo comunitario del asma y en el desarrollo de modelos innovadores de atenci&amp;oacute;n que reducen las desigualdades en salud. Como ponente de Columbia en esta conferencia virtual internacional, presentar&amp;aacute; sobre el asma y el rol de los trabajadores comunitarios de la salud en la conexi&amp;oacute;n entre la educaci&amp;oacute;n cl&amp;iacute;nica y los recursos centrados en el paciente y la comunidad.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;----&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This international medical virtual conference&amp;nbsp;brings together partners from Columbia University Irving Medical Center and Universidad Nacional Pedro Henr&amp;iacute;quez Ure&amp;ntilde;a for a cross-cultural conversation on mental and respiratory health. UNPHU will explore depression and anxiety, including stigma and cultural perspectives, while CUIMC will highlight asthma and the role of community health workers in connecting education, care, and community resources. This conference will occur in Spanish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Kersy Yoirys Medina F&amp;eacute;liz&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a psychiatrist and UNPHU faculty member with advanced training in Internal Medicine, Psychiatry, family therapy, and addiction. She currently serves as Manager of the Mental Health Department at the Vinicio Calventi Teaching Hospital and brings extensive experience in clinical care, academic teaching, and mental health leadership. As the UNPHU speaker for this international wellness lecture, she will present on depression and anxiety, with a focus on mental health stigma and cultural perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Luz Adriana Matiz&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a Professor of Pediatrics at Columbia University Irving Medical Center and Medical Director of NewYork Presbyterian Hospital&amp;rsquo;s Center for Community Health Navigation, where she leads system wide patient navigator and community health worker programs. She brings nationally recognized expertise in community based asthma care and innovative care delivery models that address health disparities. As the Columbia speaker for this international wellness lecture, she will present on asthma and the role of community health workers in connecting clinical education with patient centered and community based resources.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alexandre de La Patelliere and Matthieu Delaporte, 2024, 168 min.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marseille, 1815. All of young Edmond Dant&amp;egrave;s&amp;rsquo; dreams are about to come true &amp;ndash;promoted to ship&amp;rsquo;s captain he can finally marry the love of his life, Mercedes. But his success inspires jealousy from various quarters. Betrayed by his rivals and denounced as a member of a pro-Bonaparte conspiracy, he is imprisoned without trial at the Ch&amp;acirc;teau d&amp;rsquo;If, with no hope of return.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After fourteen years of secret instruction by fellow inmate Abb&amp;eacute; Faria, Dant&amp;egrave;s manages to escape and to get hold of the legendary treasure hidden on the isle of Monte Cristo. Now with a huge fortune, he hatches an extraordinary plan to exact the vengeance he craves. Assuming multiple identities &amp;ndash;&amp;ldquo;the Count of Monte Cristo&amp;rdquo; among them &amp;ndash;Dant&amp;egrave;s first courts his enemies, now highly placed dignitaries, the better to strike them down. But the price of revenge is heavy for one&amp;rsquo;s soul.&lt;/p&gt;
